From 310f0da838b37619493468fa5a76634354fe78b2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Angelo Arifi <arifilabs@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 18:54:13 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] lane-296 B1: correct run24 order-effect sign, record kernel
 identity R vs U8

First leg of a round runs ~2% slower, so run24's hoist block (r86i always first) favoured U8; the sx8 U8-slower cells are understated, not explained. U8 mat-vec and quantize_q8_1 SPIR-V are byte-present in the r86i binary, so the iq3_xxs n=6 +3.1% is host-side, not the kernel.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Lane: lane-296
Receipts: cache/lane296/b24_resolve.py, cache/lane296/ev24
---
 .../arifi-sync/protected-win-resolutions.json | 34 +++++++++----------
 1 file changed, 17 insertions(+), 17 deletions(-)

